    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Distinct values",
      "description": "The 200 most frequent values of the selected metrics in the selected time range.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 12,
        "w": 9,
        "x": 15,
        "y": 13
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "postgres",
        "uid": "timescaledb"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "postgres",
            "uid": "timescaledb"
          },
          "format": "table",
          "rawQuery": true,
          "editorMode": "code",
          "rawSql": "SELECT met.display_name || coalesce(' ' || met.display_subname, '') || ' [' || met.metric_id || ']' AS metric,\n       coalesce(m.value_str, m.value_num::text, m.value_bool::text) AS value,\n       count(*) AS count,\n       min(m.time) AS first_seen,\n       max(m.time) AS last_seen\nFROM measurements m\nJOIN metrics met USING (metric_id)\nWHERE $__timeFilter(m.time)\n  AND m.metric_id = ANY ('{${metric:csv}}')\nGROUP BY met.metric_id, 2\nORDER BY count DESC, metric, value\nLIMIT 200"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "filterable": true
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "cellHeight": "sm",
        "showHeader": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "volkovlabs-form-panel",
      "title": "Edit: ${metric:text}",
      "description": "Definition and note of one metric. Kind: measured (sensor, meter), setting (configured by a person or the installer), state (determined by the device, such as the current room setpoint). Save writes display_name, display_subname, unit, category, kind and disabled to metrics, and the note to metric_notes; an empty note deletes it. With an empty name the definition stays as it is and only the note is saved. value_type and aggregation are not edited here: a changed type needs db/backfill_value_types.sql. Refreshing the dashboard reloads the stored values and discards what is not saved. The panel title and the Metric selector show a changed name after the page is reloaded. Needs the plugin Business Forms (volkovlabs-form-panel).",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 12,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 25
      },
      "repeat": "metric",
      "repeatDirection": "h",
      "maxPerRow": 3,
